{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-rule-induction", "file": "references/outline-interior-demo-pitfall.md", "content": "# Outlined-interior inference after rejection

When applying a fill rule to outlined shapes, classify each strict interior by its exact contents (blank, singleton marker, multiple markers, or mixed pattern) as well as dimensions. A size-to-color mapping from earlier recurrences is only a prior; current-instance evidence controls. A single demo showing blank multi-cell interiors filled with one color and a singleton interior with another supports those classes, but does not resolve test interiors with different source/background colors or patterns. After a rejected submission, do not retry by changing only the fill palette or extending the fill to more outlined regions. Request a discriminating demo if those distinctions affect the answer, then modify only classes justified by current examples; preserve all other cells.
